# Statement-coverage minimums, one area of the repository per line, enforced
# in CI by internal/tools/coverage. Raising a floor in a pull request that
# raises coverage is welcome; lowering one is never acceptable — that is the
# "coverage must not decrease" gate of AGENTS.md §3.1.
#
# Every package in the profile must fall under an area declared here, so a
# new top-level directory arrives with a decision about its floor attached
# rather than arriving unmeasured. Areas are matched by whole path segments
# and the longest one wins, so a stricter floor can be declared inside a
# broader one — "adapters/<id> 90.0" beside "adapters" holds one adapter to
# more than the aggregate does.
#
# Each floor sits just under what the area measures today: the ratchet starts
# where the code is, and only ever moves up.
adapters 88.6
cmd      92.5
internal 96.2
# internal/tools/mutate is the mutation harness: it edits sources in
# place, shells out to git and to `go test`, and its remaining branches
# are failures an earlier layer catches first — an unreadable file is
# refused as uncommitted work before the read of it is reached. It
# carries its own measured floor rather than dragging the area's.
internal/tools/mutate 90.5
